<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20837] libcfs: add tracepoints for Lustre debug messages</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20837</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The libcfs debug log (lctl debug / dk) is reliable and always&lt;br/&gt;
available, but it is poorly suited to live analysis. Messages can&lt;br/&gt;
only be read after they reach the trace buffer, filtering is limited&lt;br/&gt;
to debug masks and subsystems, and long runs of continuous logs are&lt;br/&gt;
hard to capture because the buffer wraps or is dropped under memory&lt;br/&gt;
pressure (see &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15917" title="Memory pressure prevents debug daemon / debug buffer from proper operation" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15917"&gt;LU-15917&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add kernel tracepoints (TRACE_EVENT) to libcfs_debug_msg() so that&lt;br/&gt;
external tools (bpftrace, bcc/libbpf, perf, ftrace) can capture,&lt;br/&gt;
filter and process Lustre debug messages at runtime. The existing&lt;br/&gt;
debug log is left as it is. The tracepoints cost almost nothing when&lt;br/&gt;
disabled (a static key check).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Three tracepoints are added in trace system "lustre_debug":&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre_debug_location: file, function, line, subsystem and mask&lt;br/&gt;
   of the message, emitted before formatting&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre_debug_msg: the same fields plus the formatted message text&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre_debug_msg_raw: subsystem, mask, line and message text&lt;br/&gt;
   in a ptldebug_header layout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;TP_printk output is YAML/JSON compatible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An example bcc tool, contrib/eBPF/lustre_debug_msgs.py, streams&lt;br/&gt;
messages as JSON and filters them by subsystem (-s), mask (-m),&lt;br/&gt;
source file (-f) and message count (-n), e.g.:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;python3 lustre_debug_msgs.py -s S_RPC -m D_ERROR
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is also a building block for exporting Lustre debug events to&lt;br/&gt;
OpenTelemetry pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
